    id: "directions-c2z-scent-landmark",
    situationKey: "directions",
    level: "C2",
    title: "Using smell as an unofficial landmark for the visually impaired",
    lines: [
      { speaker: "연구자", kr: "빵집 냄새나 젓갈 시장의 냄새가 시각장애인 이용자들에게 실제 이정표 역할을 한다는 걸 확인했습니다.", en: "We've confirmed that smells like a bakery's or a salted-seafood market's actually function as real landmarks for visually impaired users.", ja: "we've confirmed that smells 好き a bakery's or a salted-seafood market's actually function as real landmarks for visually impaired users.", zh: "we've confirmed that smells 喜欢 a bakery's or a salted-seafood market's actually function as real landmarks for visually impaired users.", vi: "we've confirmed that smells thích a bakery's or a salted-seafood market's actually function as real landmarks for visually impaired users." },
      { speaker: "기자", kr: "촉각이나 청각이 아니라 후각을 활용한 동선 연구는 흔치 않은데요.", en: "It's uncommon to see wayfinding research using smell rather than touch or hearing.", ja: "it's uncommon to 見る wayfinding research using smell rather than touch or hearing.", zh: "it's uncommon to 看 wayfinding research using smell rather than touch or hearing.", vi: "it's uncommon to nhìn wayfinding research using smell rather than touch or hearing." },
      { speaker: "연구자", kr: "네, 인터뷰를 해보니 냄새로 위치를 파악한다는 응답이 예상보다 훨씬 많았습니다.", en: "Right, when we interviewed people, far more responses than expected cited using smell to identify location.", ja: "正しい when we interviewed 人々 far more responses than expected cited using smell to identify location.", zh: "对 when we interviewed 人民 far more responses than expected cited using smell to identify location.", vi: "đúng when we interviewed người dân far more responses than expected cited using smell to identify location." },
      { speaker: "기자", kr: "그럼 이런 후각 정보를 실제 표지판 설계에도 반영할 수 있나요?", en: "Then can this olfactory information actually be incorporated into signage design?", ja: "then できる this olfactory information actually である incorporated into signage design?", zh: "then 能 this olfactory information actually 是 incorporated into signage design?", vi: "then có thể this olfactory information actually là incorporated into signage design?" },
      { speaker: "연구자", kr: "표지판 자체보다는 상점 배치나 환기구 위치를 조정해서 냄새가 특정 지점에서 뚜렷하게 나도록 유도할 수 있습니다.", en: "Rather than the signage itself, we could adjust shop placement or ventilation locations to make a smell stand out distinctly at a specific point.", ja: "rather than the signage itself, we できた adjust shop placement or ventilation locations to 作る a smell stand out distinctly at a specific point.", zh: "rather than the signage itself, we 可以 adjust shop placement or ventilation locations to 做 a smell stand out distinctly at a specific point.", vi: "rather than the signage itself, we có thể adjust shop placement or ventilation locations to làm a smell stand out distinctly at a specific point." },
      { speaker: "기자", kr: "그런데 상점이 바뀌면 그 후각 이정표도 함께 사라지는 거 아닌가요?", en: "But if the shop changes, wouldn't that olfactory landmark disappear along with it?", ja: "(But if the shop changes, wouldn't t...)", zh: "(But if the shop changes, wouldn't t...)", vi: "(But if the shop changes, wouldn't t...)" },
      { speaker: "연구자", kr: "맞아요, 그게 이 방식의 한계입니다. 그래서 상권이 안정된 구간에만 우선 적용하는 걸 권고하고 있어요.", en: "That's right, that's the limitation of this approach. So we're recommending it be applied first only to sections with a stable commercial district.", ja: "that's 正しい that's the limitation of this approach. so we're recommending it である applied first only to sections with a stable commercial district.", zh: "that's 对 that's the limitation of this approach. so we're recommending it 是 applied first only to sections with a stable commercial district.", vi: "that's đúng that's the limitation of this approach. so we're recommending it là applied first only to sections with a stable commercial district." },
      { speaker: "기자", kr: "장기적으로는 인공 향을 특정 구간에 배치하는 방안도 검토 중이신가요?", en: "In the long term, are you also considering placing artificial scents at specific sections?", ja: "in the 長い term, です you also considering placing artificial scents at specific sections?", zh: "in the 长 term, 是 you also considering placing artificial scents at specific sections?", vi: "in the dài term, là you also considering placing artificial scents at specific sections?" },
      { speaker: "연구자", kr: "검토는 하고 있지만, 인공 향은 자연스럽지 않다는 반발이 있어서 신중하게 접근하고 있습니다.", en: "We are reviewing it, but there's pushback that artificial scent feels unnatural, so we're approaching it cautiously.", ja: "we です reviewing it, but there's pushback that artificial scent feels unnatural, so we're approaching it cautiously.", zh: "we 是 reviewing it, but there's pushback that artificial scent feels unnatural, so we're approaching it cautiously.", vi: "we là reviewing it, but there's pushback that artificial scent feels unnatural, so we're approaching it cautiously." },
    ],
